00:51:05,325 --> 00:51:07,259
- There you go.
- Thanks.

497
00:51:13,767 --> 00:51:14,961
Carrie!

498
00:51:16,603 --> 00:51:19,970
I'm sorry.
She's just already got it all figured out.

499
00:51:22,376 --> 00:51:23,570
Nicole.

500
00:51:24,511 --> 00:51:26,479
- I remember.
- Really?

501
00:51:28,582 --> 00:51:29,844
I remember your daughter.

502
00:51:30,217 --> 00:51:32,378
Well, she's hard to forget.

503
00:51:44,498 --> 00:51:46,989
Luke was supposed to bring this home.

504
00:51:47,100 --> 00:51:49,227
He has his father's memory.

505
00:51:50,170 --> 00:51:54,436
It's for Carrie's birthday party.
Please, come. I'd love to meet your wife.

506
00:51:55,809 --> 00:51:57,572
She won't be there.

507
00:51:59,046 --> 00:52:00,707
It's complicated.

508
00:52:02,315 --> 00:52:04,545
I understand. With me, too.

509
00:52:07,554 --> 00:52:09,078
Carrie, come on, let's go.

510
00:52:10,190 --> 00:52:13,648
We're gonna grab a bite to eat.
Would you like to come?

511
00:52:14,094 --> 00:52:16,961
- No, I don't... We're kind of...
- Busy?

512
00:52:19,699 --> 00:52:22,259
Come on. We owe you for the cookies.

513
00:52:24,805 --> 00:52:25,829
Well, that's true.

514
00:52:26,339 --> 00:52:28,307
And I did make those cookies myself.

515
00:52:28,408 --> 00:52:30,399
And learned how to pre-package them.

516
00:52:37,117 --> 00:52:38,277
Come on, Luke.

517
00:52:41,221 --> 00:52:43,689
So, do you trade off time with Luke?

518
00:52:43,790 --> 00:52:46,452
No, Luke and I are together full-time.

519
00:52:46,560 --> 00:52:49,688
Wow. I guess that's why I see you so much.

520
00:52:50,530 --> 00:52:53,988
She'd like nothing better than to be here,
with him.

521
00:52:54,101 --> 00:52:57,298
Lara, she... She misses all this.

522
00:52:59,506 --> 00:53:01,201
I guess it's all about priorities, isn't it?

523
00:53:06,480 --> 00:53:08,471
No, she's not like that.

524
00:53:09,683 --> 00:53:11,378
She's in prison.

525
00:53:15,288 --> 00:53:17,722
- I don't tell most people.
- I understand.

526
00:53:17,824 --> 00:53:19,553
She's innocent. She didn't kill that woman.

527
00:53:20,994 --> 00:53:23,019
Good. I mean...

528
00:53:24,297 --> 00:53:26,128
I'm sure she didn't.

529
00:53:28,902 --> 00:53:31,234
We really should be going home.

530
00:53:31,338 --> 00:53:32,532
Okay.

531
00:53:33,340 --> 00:53:36,639
Thank you very much for the invitation.
We'll try and make it.

532
00:53:36,743 --> 00:53:38,506
That would be great.

533
00:53:38,879 --> 00:53:40,938
- Goodbye. Luke!
- Bye.

534
00:53:41,848 --> 00:53:43,110
Come on.

535
00:53:50,690 --> 00:53:52,317
Carrie, come on!

536
00:57:23,436 --> 00:57:24,630
- Hey.
- Hey.

537
00:57:24,738 --> 00:57:26,228
What's wrong?

538
00:57:27,907 --> 00:57:29,306
What is it?

539
00:57:36,583 --> 00:57:37,641
No.

540
00:57:38,151 --> 00:57:39,209
No.

541
00:57:40,653 --> 00:57:42,951
They can't move you without notice.

542
00:57:43,056 --> 00:57:45,047
Three days isn't notice.

543
00:57:45,658 --> 00:57:49,389
I was only here through the appeal.
We knew I was going to a prison.

544
00:57:53,900 --> 00:57:57,597
No, no, I don't have two weeks.
I gotta close the escrow tomorrow.

545
00:57:57,704 --> 00:58:00,502
Well, the title hasn't even been cleared yet.
I mean, there's no way I can...

546
00:58:00,607 --> 00:58:01,801
How much can they give me?

547
00:58:02,308 --> 00:58:03,332
Nothing!

548
00:58:32,872 --> 00:58:33,998
What are you doing here?

549
00:58:34,674 --> 00:58:35,732
I've got class.

550
00:58:39,012 --> 00:58:40,707
You be good, okay?

551
00:58:44,884 --> 00:58:45,873
Thanks.

552
00:59:59,726 --> 01:00:00,920
Are you okay? You're okay?

553
01:00:01,027 --> 01:00:02,358
- Are you okay?
- What are you doing?

554
01:00:02,462 --> 01:00:03,622
You almost killed us!

555
01:00:03,730 --> 01:00:04,788
I'm so, so sorry.

556
01:00:04,898 --> 01:00:06,627
You're out of your mind. You don't look.

557
01:00:07,534 --> 01:00:09,832
Get away. Get away from us!

558
01:00:44,270 --> 01:00:45,362
Hey.

559
01:00:51,044 --> 01:00:52,636
What's wrong?

560
01:00:52,745 --> 01:00:53,712
Nothing.

561
01:00:54,147 --> 01:00:55,478
Is it Luke?

562
01:00:55,582 --> 01:00:57,015
- No.
- What?

563
01:01:01,054 --> 01:01:03,545
I... I asked Meyer

564
01:01:04,123 --> 01:01:06,591
to look into not having you moved.

565
01:01:08,595 --> 01:01:12,554
I told him that traveling that distance
would be a hardship on us,

566
01:01:12,665 --> 01:01:14,724
that Luke was already having problems
at school, which is true.

567
01:01:14,834 --> 01:01:16,825
I haven't been spending
enough time with him.

568
01:01:17,403 --> 01:01:18,768
You haven't?

569
01:01:19,105 --> 01:01:20,197
No.

570
01:01:21,140 --> 01:01:22,573
You haven't?

571
01:01:25,812 --> 01:01:27,279
Jesus, John.

572
01:01:29,349 --> 01:01:31,374
You really are too much.

573
01:01:31,951 --> 01:01:36,320
Luke is having a hard time,
because Mommy's in jail for murder,

574
01:01:36,422 --> 01:01:39,789
not because Daddy doesn't spend
enough time with him.

575
01:01:41,394 --> 01:01:44,522
Your father was right. You really don't
live in the same world we do.

576
01:01:46,933 --> 01:01:49,595
That's nice, that the two of you talk.

577
01:01:50,870 --> 01:01:52,394
What world do I live in, Lara?

578
01:01:52,505 --> 01:01:55,065
Well, I don't know, John,
but it's not the real one.

579
01:01:55,174 --> 01:01:57,438
The one in which I'm in here
for the rest of my life.

580
01:01:57,543 --> 01:02:01,138
So don't be talking to me about fantasies
like there's some happily ever...

581
01:02:01,447 --> 01:02:02,937
We good here?

582
01:02:05,952 --> 01:02:07,613
Yes. Sorry.

583
01:02:20,466 --> 01:02:23,196
Now you're gonna sit here all long-faced,
like you let me down.

584
01:02:23,302 --> 01:02:26,135
I mean, what do you want me to do here?
You want me to make you feel better?

585
01:02:26,239 --> 01:02:27,433
Got it.

586
01:02:28,374 --> 01:02:29,739
I'm sorry.

587
01:02:29,842 --> 01:02:31,400
Now you're apologizing.

588
01:02:31,511 --> 01:02:33,445
You really are a gem.

589
01:02:33,546 --> 01:02:36,674
- What do you want from me, Lara?
- What do I want from you? Nothing.

590
01:02:36,783 --> 01:02:38,478
You're already too perfect.

591
01:02:39,419 --> 01:02:41,614
You know,
you never even asked me if I did it.

592
01:02:42,522 --> 01:02:44,752
- If I killed her.
- Because I know you didn't.

593
01:02:44,857 --> 01:02:46,882
Well, then you'd be wrong.

594
01:03:00,940 --> 01:03:02,373
I'm done.

595
01:03:37,844 --> 01:03:39,971
Sir, you can't stand there.

596
01:03:40,747 --> 01:03:43,580
Sir, I need you to leave the building now.

597
01:03:44,317 --> 01:03:45,409
Sir?

598
01:04:02,802 --> 01:04:04,394
- What?
- Shut up.

599
01:04:05,838 --> 01:04:09,069
I don't care what you say or how you say it.

600
01:04:10,843 --> 01:04:12,401
I don't believe you did it.

601
01:04:14,213 --> 01:04:15,908
And I never will.

602
01:04:20,419 --> 01:04:22,319
I know who you are.

603
01:04:24,757 --> 01:04:26,725
And I promise you

604
01:04:28,394 --> 01:04:30,555
this will not be your life.

605
01:07:45,825 --> 01:07:47,053
Shut up!

606
01:08:00,206 --> 01:08:02,197
- I don't know what's going on, man.
- You done?

607
01:08:02,308 --> 01:08:03,275
Everybody is out.

608
01:08:03,376 --> 01:08:05,276
I gotta get back to Jimmy.

609
01:08:07,546 --> 01:08:09,514
Back away! Back away!

610
01:08:12,318 --> 01:08:13,376
Drop the gun! Drop it!

611
01:08:13,753 --> 01:08:15,118
Put the dog away!

612
01:08:15,221 --> 01:08:16,552
You shoot the dog, I'll kill you!

613
01:08:17,723 --> 01:08:19,816
- You want the police here, asshole?
- Good idea!

614
01:08:23,396 --> 01:08:24,522
Get in, get in, get in!

615
01:08:24,630 --> 01:08:26,188
- You, too!
- I'm not getting in there!

616
01:08:26,298 --> 01:08:27,925
Get in there!

617
01:08:28,034 --> 01:08:29,001
Get in! Get in! Get in!

618
01:08:31,337 --> 01:08:33,828
All right, lock it. Lock the door.

619
01:08:36,075 --> 01:08:37,508
- Move!
- You are dead.

620
01:08:37,610 --> 01:08:39,407
- I didn't do anything.
- You brought him here!

621
01:08:39,512 --> 01:08:40,979
I didn't bring him!

622
01:08:42,915 --> 01:08:45,145
On your knees! On the floor!

623
01:08:52,925 --> 01:08:54,620
All right. Where's your money?

624
01:08:56,996 --> 01:08:59,487
Here. It's worth it to get rid of you.

625
01:08:59,899 --> 01:09:01,389
- Where's the rest?
- Here.

626
01:09:02,134 --> 01:09:03,965
- Take more.
- Where do you keep your money?

627
01:09:04,070 --> 01:09:05,867
I'm gonna give my money to you. Yeah.

628
01:09:05,971 --> 01:09:07,939
- I'll shoot you.
- You can't even shoot a dog.

629
01:09:08,040 --> 01:09:09,701
- I'll kill you both!
- No, I'm gonna kill you both!

630
01:09:09,809 --> 01:09:12,607
- Just give him your money!
- Keep your dead bitch mouth shut!

631
01:09:12,711 --> 01:09:13,678
Give him your money!

632
01:09:14,180 --> 01:09:15,169
Jesus!

633
01:09:20,820 --> 01:09:23,050
See? You ain't gonna kill me.

634
01:09:24,623 --> 01:09:25,783
This is the worst you could do?

635
01:09:27,126 --> 01:09:30,892
Go home.
I'll come, I'll find you and I'll kill you.

636
01:09:40,005 --> 01:09:41,996
You're wasting some good shit there!

637
01:09:42,108 --> 01:09:43,075
Yeah, good shit.

638
01:09:43,309 --> 01:09:44,401
High alcohol content.

639
01:09:50,616 --> 01:09:52,049
What are you gonna do?
You gonna burn me out?

640
01:09:52,284 --> 01:09:54,377
Yeah. That's what I'm gonna do.

641
01:09:54,487 --> 01:09:55,511
Jesus Christ!

642
01:09:55,621 --> 01:09:57,418
This is a meth lab, you idiot!

643
01:09:57,857 --> 01:09:58,949
No.

644
01:09:59,692 --> 01:10:00,989
It was.

645
01:10:02,895 --> 01:10:04,157
Tell me! Where's your money?

646
01:10:04,263 --> 01:10:05,992
My kid is upstairs!

647
01:10:06,732 --> 01:10:08,097
My kid is upstairs!

648
01:10:10,302 --> 01:10:11,462
- Get up!
- Jesus!

649
01:10:11,570 --> 01:10:12,764
Get up!

650
01:10:33,692 --> 01:10:34,886
Please.

651
01:10:36,262 --> 01:10:38,025
Please, let me go, please.

652
01:11:18,003 --> 01:11:19,470
Anybody here?

653
01:11:47,233 --> 01:11:48,996
Don't leave me here.

654
01:11:50,102 --> 01:11:51,763
I don't wanna die here.

655
01:11:57,109 --> 01:11:58,201
Please!

656
01:12:33,812 --> 01:12:35,871
Please, get me to a hospital!

657
01:12:38,550 --> 01:12:40,108
I can't breathe.

658
01:12:45,624 --> 01:12:46,852
Please.

659
01:12:53,799 --> 01:12:55,460
I can't breathe.

660
01:13:00,439 --> 01:13:02,430
I can't... I can't...

661
01:14:16,315 --> 01:14:18,010
Get out of my way.

662
01:14:23,756 --> 01:14:25,986
- What do we have?
- A freaking miracle.

663
01:14:26,091 --> 01:14:28,855
Meth lab in the basement,
the house still standing.

664
01:14:28,961 --> 01:14:30,690
Should be just a crater.

665
01:14:30,796 --> 01:14:31,888
We know him?

666
01:14:31,997 --> 01:14:35,433
Alex Gaidar,
history of violence and drug trafficking.

667
01:14:45,177 --> 01:14:46,439
He have a kid?

668
01:14:46,545 --> 01:14:48,740
Neighbor said wife left with him last year.

669
01:14:49,148 --> 01:14:50,911
Big surprise there.

670
01:14:51,316 --> 01:14:52,943
And this blood,

671
01:14:55,721 --> 01:14:57,245
they type it all yet?

672
01:14:57,356 --> 01:15:00,382
No, but someone left through
the back door bleeding.

673
01:15:00,492 --> 01:15:04,121
Zone Three found a gunshot victim dead
on a transit bench.

674
01:15:50,442 --> 01:15:51,409
Hey.

675
01:15:53,745 --> 01:15:55,372
I've just come to pick up Luke.

676
01:15:55,481 --> 01:15:57,073
He's sound asleep.

677
01:15:59,818 --> 01:16:02,218
Yeah, I've just come to get Luke.

678
01:16:07,092 --> 01:16:08,059
John.

679
01:16:11,363 --> 01:16:13,058
Are you all right?

680
01:16:13,765 --> 01:16:15,323
Yeah. I'm fine.

681
01:16:26,011 --> 01:16:27,376
Hey, buddy.

682
01:16:27,779 --> 01:16:30,111
Wake up, bud, we're going home.

683
01:17:33,445 --> 01:17:34,810
So, what do you say?

684
01:17:35,681 --> 01:17:37,672
Thank you, Grandma.

685
01:17:37,783 --> 01:17:39,444
I think you should give Grandma a big kiss.

686
01:17:39,551 --> 01:17:41,644
- I'm too tired for kisses.
- Buddy.

687
01:17:41,753 --> 01:17:45,587
That's okay.
I'll get lots of kisses next weekend.

688
01:17:46,091 --> 01:17:48,389
We want to take him
to the Fall Festival in Kutztown

689
01:17:48,493 --> 01:17:50,461
where the Clydesdales are.

690
01:17:54,700 --> 01:17:56,429
- See you.
- Bye.

691
01:17:58,570 --> 01:17:59,628
Bye.

692
01:18:01,506 --> 01:18:02,632
Hey.

693
01:18:06,678 --> 01:18:08,441
- Bye, Grandpa.
- Bye.

694
01:18:25,964 --> 01:18:27,226
Goodbye.

695
01:18:39,277 --> 01:18:40,539
Bye, Mom.

696
01:18:40,979 --> 01:18:42,071
Bye.

697
01:19:02,813 --> 01:19:04,940
You're getting sentimental in your old age.

698
01:19:05,882 --> 01:19:07,076
Yeah.

699
01:19:10,287 --> 01:19:11,914
Well, might as well have some coffee.

700
01:19:35,779 --> 01:19:37,144
Yo! Idiots!

701
01:19:41,651 --> 01:19:43,278
Can I carry him?

702
01:19:43,787 --> 01:19:46,551
No, bud. Only what fits in the bag, all right?

703
01:19:52,395 --> 01:19:54,158
What about my pockets?

704
01:19:54,264 --> 01:19:55,856
Or your pockets.

705
01:21:24,654 --> 01:21:25,621
Hello?

706
01:21:28,425 --> 01:21:29,619
Hello?

707
01:21:53,917 --> 01:21:56,613
Bud? I'll be back in a moment, okay?

708
01:21:56,720 --> 01:21:57,687
Okay.

709
01:22:32,322 --> 01:22:33,755
Hey, bud.

710
01:22:34,791 --> 01:22:35,917
So...

711
01:22:37,560 --> 01:22:38,527
You all right?

712
01:22:39,496 --> 01:22:40,588
Yeah.

713
01:22:43,333 --> 01:22:44,891
They're calling all the party animals.

714
01:22:45,368 --> 01:22:47,734
922 Yetta Street.

715
01:22:48,638 --> 01:22:49,605
I know where that is.

716
01:22:50,140 --> 01:22:52,131
Okay? Here we go.

717
01:23:10,961 --> 01:23:14,192
Yeah, taillight matches
any 2004 to 2009 Prius.

718
01:23:15,198 --> 01:23:16,961
What kind of criminal drives a Prius?

719
01:23:17,067 --> 01:23:18,398
A socially responsible one.

720
01:23:19,169 --> 01:23:22,332
There's over 1,000 registered in the city,
7,000 in the state.

721
01:23:23,006 --> 01:23:25,998
- How many are registered to felons?
- Six in the state.

722
01:23:26,109 --> 01:23:30,409
Four to embezzlers, white-collar criminals,
one to a rapist, one to a murderer.

723
01:23:30,513 --> 01:23:33,277
- Start with the murderer.
- She's in prison for life.

724
01:23:33,750 --> 01:23:34,739
Rapist is out.

725
01:23:38,788 --> 01:23:40,050
Find him.

726
01:23:41,658 --> 01:23:42,886
Come on.

727
01:23:47,998 --> 01:23:49,488
- Hello.
- Hi.

728
01:23:50,734 --> 01:23:52,725
- Good to see you.
- It's good to see you, too.

729
01:23:56,906 --> 01:23:59,431
- Hi, Luke.
- It's a pony.

730
01:24:00,343 --> 01:24:02,402
Those aren't easy to wrap.

731
01:24:05,115 --> 01:24:07,845
- You know the party is not until 11:00, right?
- Really?

732
01:24:09,152 --> 01:24:13,350
What is it? Around 9:00? I'm sorry.
I should've read it more carefully.

733
01:24:13,456 --> 01:24:16,948
It's no problem.
Why don't you go give this to Carrie?

734
01:24:20,730 --> 01:24:21,754
Well, I guess you can help.

735
01:24:22,098 --> 01:24:24,123
Actually, I've gotta go
and run some errands.

736
01:24:25,235 --> 01:24:26,202
Sorry.

737
01:24:29,606 --> 01:24:30,868
We'll see you later then.

738
01:24:32,308 --> 01:24:33,866
Thanks so much.

739
01:24:39,182 --> 01:24:41,480
He has my parents' phone number.

740
01:24:42,252 --> 01:24:44,982
In his jacket. Top pocket of his jacket.

741
01:24:47,757 --> 01:24:49,554
If I'm running late.

742
01:24:50,326 --> 01:24:51,725
No problem.

743
01:25:02,205 --> 01:25:05,538
The rapist is in a wheelchair.
Not sure if that was karma or just bad luck.

744
01:25:05,642 --> 01:25:07,803
The murderer. Where is she incarcerated?

745
01:25:07,911 --> 01:25:09,435
County, right here in town.

746
01:25:09,546 --> 01:25:12,913
Does she have a husband
or a kid old enough to drive?

747
01:25:27,097 --> 01:25:28,496
Yes? What?

748
01:25:29,065 --> 01:25:31,124
Lara Brennan's blood work.

749
01:25:34,437 --> 01:25:35,734
Get the lab.

750
01:25:42,512 --> 01:25:45,345
You pissed somebody off, that's for sure.

751
01:25:50,220 --> 01:25:53,246
- It's still busy. I'll keep trying.
- No. Get an ambulance.

752
01:25:53,723 --> 01:25:57,284
Take her to University Hospital.
I'll meet them there.

753
01:25:58,962 --> 01:26:01,089
Right. Thanks.

754
01:26:01,731 --> 01:26:02,857
Husband, schoolteacher.

755
01:26:03,633 --> 01:26:05,624
You got a home address?

756
01:27:11,801 --> 01:27:14,668
No car in the garage.
You want to get a warrant?

757
01:27:14,771 --> 01:27:15,897
Yeah.

758
01:27:46,069 --> 01:27:47,468
Get the warrant.

759
01:28:30,713 --> 01:28:33,409
Lara Brennan's being transferred
to University Hospital.

760
01:28:33,516 --> 01:28:34,915
- Right now?
- Right now.

761
01:28:35,551 --> 01:28:37,246
Have them call the escort vehicle.

762
01:28:37,353 --> 01:28:39,253
Tell them we'll meet them at the hospital
in less than 10.

763
01:28:43,693 --> 01:28:47,652
Yeah. Yeah, we're here.
Prisoner's secure. No problems.

764
01:28:49,198 --> 01:28:50,460
Will do.

765
01:28:52,135 --> 01:28:53,102
Hands where I can see 'em.

766
01:28:53,536 --> 01:28:54,503
John?

767
01:28:54,604 --> 01:28:55,832
And the phone.

768
01:28:56,172 --> 01:28:57,298
What are you doing here, John?

769
01:28:57,407 --> 01:28:58,601
Put your hands on your head.

770
01:28:59,475 --> 01:29:00,806
John, what are you doing?

771
01:29:01,177 --> 01:29:03,145
Uncuff her. Kneel down.

772
01:29:05,014 --> 01:29:06,675
John, stop this.

773
01:29:07,784 --> 01:29:09,081
Kneel down. Face the wall.

774
01:29:14,757 --> 01:29:16,418
Unit 2242 secure,

775
01:29:17,226 --> 01:29:19,057
- She just said...
- Just take the light.

776
01:29:24,600 --> 01:29:26,192
Hands and feet, pull 'em as tight as you can.

777
01:29:26,302 --> 01:29:29,601
You walk out that door with him,
you will both be dead.

778
01:29:29,706 --> 01:29:31,105
- Shut up.
- John, he's right.

779
01:29:31,207 --> 01:29:33,505
Listen to him. You're gonna get us killed.

780
01:29:33,609 --> 01:29:36,100
- Why are you doing this?
- Because we have no other choice!

781
01:29:36,212 --> 01:29:37,577
- Put 'em on.
- No. That's not true!

782
01:29:37,680 --> 01:29:38,942
- Put the clothes on, Lara.
- No.

783
01:29:39,048 --> 01:29:40,481
- Now!
- No!

784
01:29:41,484 --> 01:29:42,473
Okay.

785
01:29:43,186 --> 01:29:46,246
You call your son
and tell him you're not coming.

786
01:29:46,356 --> 01:29:47,584
- Where is he?
- He's waiting for you.

787
01:29:47,690 --> 01:29:48,918
You wanna tell him you're not coming?

788
01:29:49,359 --> 01:29:51,088
- How can you do this to me?
- Push "send."

789
01:29:51,194 --> 01:29:52,525
Tell him I'm not coming, either.

790
01:29:53,296 --> 01:29:55,662
- John.
- Does it look like I'm going home, Lara?

791
01:29:56,499 --> 01:30:01,368
You call him, tell him he's alone now
and his mom and dad are not coming back.

792
01:30:03,106 --> 01:30:04,573
Jesus, John.

793
01:30:05,975 --> 01:30:07,738
You son of a bitch.

794
01:30:20,590 --> 01:30:23,354
I'm Dr. Lifson.
You've got a patient here from County Jail.

795
01:30:23,459 --> 01:30:24,448
Lara Brennan?

796
01:30:24,560 --> 01:30:27,927
Yes, we started an IV.
D50 with 20 units of insulin.

797
01:30:35,972 --> 01:30:36,961
Copy.

798
01:30:44,414 --> 01:30:45,676
Security!

799
01:30:46,849 --> 01:30:47,941
Security!

800
01:30:50,553 --> 01:30:51,884
Out! Out!

801
01:31:20,516 --> 01:31:21,676
- Hey, hey.
- Back away!

802
01:31:21,784 --> 01:31:22,978
- Now don't be stupid.
- You stay back!

803
01:31:23,085 --> 01:31:26,020
We have units at every exit, John.
You will be shot trying to leave.

804
01:31:26,122 --> 01:31:27,089
Hit the button, Lara.

805
01:31:27,190 --> 01:31:28,657
- Stop.
- Hit the button!

806
01:31:28,758 --> 01:31:30,521
John, do not do this.

807
01:31:31,627 --> 01:31:33,959
- Where are the stairs?
- There.

808
01:31:34,063 --> 01:31:36,964
Male and female, white lab coats,
parking levels.

809
01:31:38,167 --> 01:31:40,192
Hey. It's gonna be okay.

810
01:31:42,371 --> 01:31:45,204
Look at me, look at me.
Everything's gonna be okay.

811
01:31:45,308 --> 01:31:48,971
Just do what I say when I say it.
Everything will be okay.

812
01:31:49,479 --> 01:31:51,879
Lara, take the coat off.

813
01:31:53,282 --> 01:31:54,271
Come on.

814
01:31:57,286 --> 01:31:59,015
It's okay. You stay here.

815
01:31:59,121 --> 01:32:00,213
All security personnel...

816
01:32:12,735 --> 01:32:14,532
- Watch the door!
- Yeah.

817
01:32:48,404 --> 01:32:49,530
Stop.

818
01:32:50,406 --> 01:32:51,566
Shit.

819
01:32:52,575 --> 01:32:53,564
Who's in the lobby?

820
01:32:56,946 --> 01:32:59,141
Hey, listen. Is anybody in the lobby?

821
01:33:15,398 --> 01:33:16,831
Don't look.

822
01:33:19,335 --> 01:33:20,324
Run!

823
01:33:22,572 --> 01:33:23,561
Great!

824
01:33:23,673 --> 01:33:24,640
Back here!

825
01:33:30,079 --> 01:33:31,068
Move.

826
01:33:34,650 --> 01:33:36,379
Let's get moving!

827
01:33:40,289 --> 01:33:41,551
Come on.

828
01:33:47,830 --> 01:33:48,990
Here!

829
01:34:04,480 --> 01:34:05,742
Hey, hey!

830
01:34:11,520 --> 01:34:12,919
Go Penguins!

831
01:34:13,022 --> 01:34:14,751
Let your hair down.

832
01:34:23,265 --> 01:34:25,529
Harris, that way. Go!

833
01:34:41,117 --> 01:34:42,209
Hey!

834
01:34:58,000 --> 01:35:01,299
Harris, they're in the subway.
Harris! The subway!

835
01:35:01,404 --> 01:35:02,371
Got it.

836
01:35:14,850 --> 01:35:15,839
They're on the platform!

837
01:35:15,951 --> 01:35:20,047
Block stations in either directions!
Call the Port Authority. Stop all the trains!

838
01:35:35,171 --> 01:35:36,695
Wait, wait, wait.

839
01:35:37,707 --> 01:35:39,402
What are we doing?

840
01:35:42,778 --> 01:35:45,576
Stand clear of the closing doors, please,

841
01:35:48,951 --> 01:35:50,816
Move! Pittsburgh PD!

842
01:35:52,388 --> 01:35:56,154
The train on track four, I want it stopped.
Stop that train!

843
01:36:09,205 --> 01:36:11,173
Next stop...

844
01:36:47,309 --> 01:36:48,367
Hold on to me.

845
01:36:48,477 --> 01:36:50,104
Hey, kid, two hands.

846
01:37:03,459 --> 01:37:04,790
No. No.

847
01:37:13,602 --> 01:37:14,569
This way.

848
01:37:16,705 --> 01:37:17,694
There.

849
01:38:03,118 --> 01:38:04,244
- Red light.
- Hold on.

850
01:38:04,353 --> 01:38:05,718
Red light!

851
01:38:30,145 --> 01:38:32,807
Ring the city. Close bus and train stations.

852
01:38:32,915 --> 01:38:34,974
And get their description
to the state police.

853
01:38:35,084 --> 01:38:36,051
Copy that,

854
01:38:36,151 --> 01:38:38,483
- How old is their damn kid?
- Six.

855
01:38:38,954 --> 01:38:40,854
Find out where he is.

856
01:38:45,794 --> 01:38:47,955
- Why didn't you tell me?
- You would've stopped me.

857
01:38:49,398 --> 01:38:51,161
Your insulin is in here.

858
01:38:51,267 --> 01:38:53,792
There's a case in here.
It's got a brush, moisturizer, makeup.

859
01:38:53,903 --> 01:38:56,838
Everything you had was old.
I hope I got it right.

860
01:39:06,782 --> 01:39:09,114
You remember where you last saw him?

861
01:39:09,218 --> 01:39:12,187
You want to take a guess
who just escaped from jail?

862
01:39:12,288 --> 01:39:13,312
Hold on a second.

863
01:39:19,361 --> 01:39:21,761
- Hello.
- Hi. I'm here to pick up my son.

864
01:39:21,864 --> 01:39:23,126
They aren't back yet.

865
01:39:24,667 --> 01:39:26,191
Back from where?

866
01:39:26,302 --> 01:39:27,792
From the zoo.

867
01:39:31,006 --> 01:39:32,200
It's a zoo party.

868
01:39:33,842 --> 01:39:36,868
They should be back in about an hour
if you'd like to wait.

869
01:39:36,979 --> 01:39:38,469
No. Thank you.

870
01:39:42,952 --> 01:39:44,977
What's wrong? What is it?

871
01:39:46,188 --> 01:39:48,622
- Where is he? Where's Luke?
- He's at the party.

872
01:39:48,724 --> 01:39:50,521
What party? You said the party was here.

873
01:39:50,626 --> 01:39:53,459
I was wrong. She's taken them to the zoo.

874
01:39:55,464 --> 01:39:58,456
- Destination, Pittsburgh Zoo,
- She?

875
01:39:59,001 --> 01:40:02,630
Estimated drive time, 17 minutes,

876
01:40:02,738 --> 01:40:04,706
Carrie's mother, Nicole.

877
01:40:26,128 --> 01:40:27,288
Check the neighbors!

878
01:40:27,396 --> 01:40:30,627
We're looking for the boy and anything
they've noticed in the last few days.

879
01:41:38,467 --> 01:41:41,493
Time to destination, 11 minutes,

880
01:41:48,477 --> 01:41:51,412
In 1,000 feet, bear left,

881
01:41:57,719 --> 01:42:01,211
In 500 feet, bear left,

882
01:42:07,729 --> 01:42:10,721
In 100 feet, bear left,

883
01:42:14,636 --> 01:42:16,001
Bear left,

884
01:42:24,012 --> 01:42:26,105
You took the wrong turn.

885
01:42:26,215 --> 01:42:27,978
John, the zoo's behind us.
You took the wrong turn.

886
01:42:28,083 --> 01:42:29,072
Babe, what are you doing?

887
01:42:29,184 --> 01:42:30,208
She'll call my parents.

888
01:42:30,686 --> 01:42:32,176
- What?
- They'll look after him,

889
01:42:32,287 --> 01:42:34,118
and I'll figure out a way of getting him to us.

890
01:42:34,223 --> 01:42:35,315
Are you out of your mind?

891
01:42:35,424 --> 01:42:36,823
I tried! There's no more time!

892
01:42:36,925 --> 01:42:38,859
Any second now,
there's gonna be a roadblock ahead of us.

893
01:42:38,961 --> 01:42:42,192
It might be there now!
If we don't get out now, we don't get out!

894
01:42:42,297 --> 01:42:45,664
I'll find a way of getting him to us, all right?
I'll find a way.

895
01:46:16,345 --> 01:46:19,508
No, really, it's fine. I just can't thank you
enough for taking care of him.

896
01:46:19,614 --> 01:46:20,774
Hey, it was our pleasure.

897
01:46:48,210 --> 01:46:49,302
Hi.

898
01:47:22,043 --> 01:47:24,409
I'm going to sit back here, okay?

899
01:47:26,448 --> 01:47:27,415
Sure.

900
01:48:09,357 --> 01:48:11,723
The traffic is backing up at the toll plazas,

901
01:48:11,827 --> 01:48:14,523
It's worse downtown where police
have cordoned off the train station

902
01:48:14,629 --> 01:48:16,426
and are searching all passengers,

903
01:48:16,531 --> 01:48:19,398
Joining us from Union Station,
our very own Sylvia Patterson,

904
01:48:19,501 --> 01:48:20,468
John?

905
01:48:25,440 --> 01:48:27,305
What are we gonna do?

906
01:48:37,619 --> 01:48:40,053
We're going to the train station.

907
01:49:22,063 --> 01:49:23,928
- Stay in the car.
- Okay.

908
01:50:06,641 --> 01:50:12,341
Sir, I'm sorry the mayor was delayed,
but I did not tell them to stop every vehicle.

909
01:50:12,447 --> 01:50:15,211
Just the ones with a couple and a child.

910
01:50:15,750 --> 01:50:17,411
Sir, I know my...

911
01:50:18,954 --> 01:50:20,285
Yes, sir.

912
01:50:58,226 --> 01:51:02,754
Are you sure $20 is enough?
Ticket to Buffalo costs three times that.

913
01:51:03,832 --> 01:51:06,892
Yeah. We're going that way anyway.

914
01:52:07,996 --> 01:52:12,695
Go wider. Send their photos to every train,
bus station and airport in a 300-mile radius.

915
01:52:12,801 --> 01:52:15,599
So Ohio, Maryland, West Virginia,

916
01:52:15,704 --> 01:52:19,401
New York, New Jersey, Virginia, Michigan,
Kentucky and Indiana?

917
01:52:20,008 --> 01:52:22,169
You know what direction they're going in,
smart-ass?

918
01:52:33,288 --> 01:52:35,756
- See you again, Tom.
- Thanks again.

919
01:52:49,871 --> 01:52:50,895
You want to see it?

920
01:52:51,206 --> 01:52:52,935
Only if it will tell me where they are.

921
01:52:53,241 --> 01:52:54,731
Not so lucky.

922
01:53:15,797 --> 01:53:18,425
Excuse me. Do you call this coffee?

923
01:53:26,674 --> 01:53:28,699
How many airports in Ontario and Quebec?

924
01:53:28,810 --> 01:53:30,778
You want me to stop calling and count?

925
01:53:32,814 --> 01:53:35,681
- Long way to go with just a carry-on.
- I'm sorry?

926
01:53:35,784 --> 01:53:38,048
Long way to go with just a carry-on.

927
01:53:39,721 --> 01:53:43,054
You know how many times
you guys have lost our bags?

928
01:53:44,025 --> 01:53:46,755
Here's your tickets and boarding passes.

929
01:53:47,796 --> 01:53:49,024
Thank you.

930
01:53:52,200 --> 01:53:53,360
They found the parents.

931
01:54:17,792 --> 01:54:21,250
You decided to go for a drive
for the entire day?

932
01:54:21,696 --> 01:54:23,960
George wanted to see the leaves.

933
01:54:39,480 --> 01:54:42,381
And you have absolutely no idea
where they're going, right?

934
01:54:42,483 --> 01:54:44,576
I told you. We never spoke.

935
01:55:12,547 --> 01:55:13,571
Hey.

936
01:55:15,984 --> 01:55:17,451
I'll do this.

937
01:55:27,862 --> 01:55:29,193
Go ahead, Luke.

938
01:55:32,033 --> 01:55:33,000
Hello.

939
01:55:47,081 --> 01:55:49,641
You look like you need to get away.

940
01:56:00,028 --> 01:56:01,359
Thank you.

941
01:56:03,598 --> 01:56:05,156
Come on, buddy.

942
01:56:35,563 --> 01:56:38,396
- Too bad you didn't find more of it.
- Yeah.

943
01:56:39,500 --> 01:56:41,798
And I wish I could figure out where this is.

944
01:56:42,570 --> 01:56:45,562
I checked Web sites for every
tourist destination I could think of.

945
01:56:46,941 --> 01:56:49,171
- That's the Presidential Palace.
- What?

946
01:56:49,277 --> 01:56:52,576
It was all over CNN
when it collapsed during the earthquake.

947
01:56:56,250 --> 01:56:57,877
We know where they're going!

948
01:56:57,986 --> 01:56:59,214
Show me.

949
01:57:00,355 --> 01:57:03,950
Thank you for waiting,
We'll soon begin boarding by rows,

950
01:57:07,562 --> 01:57:10,156
Hold them at the gate. Take a look.

951
01:57:11,499 --> 01:57:12,796
Let's go!

952
01:57:34,255 --> 01:57:36,382
Excuse me, folks. No one else on.

953
01:57:37,058 --> 01:57:40,186
Excuse me, folks. Excuse me.
Excuse me, please.

954
01:57:58,413 --> 01:58:01,143
Sorry. There's no one by that description
on this flight.

955
01:58:01,449 --> 01:58:03,041
No. They're on it.

956
01:58:03,151 --> 01:58:04,345
Do you have the photographs?

957
01:58:04,452 --> 01:58:06,784
We have the photographs.
They're not on this plane.

958
01:58:09,424 --> 01:58:11,722
Are there any other flights to Haiti tonight?

959
01:58:11,826 --> 01:58:13,589
Are there any other flights to Haiti tonight?

960
01:58:16,030 --> 01:58:17,930
No other flights. Anything else?

961
01:58:24,072 --> 01:58:26,700
No. No. Thank you.

962
01:58:30,611 --> 01:58:31,976
It's starting to rain.

963
01:58:36,818 --> 01:58:38,513
I'll call the FBI.

964
01:58:45,126 --> 01:58:49,290
You ever ask yourself
why we found this bag and not the others?

965
01:58:58,406 --> 01:59:00,704
The captain has switched off
the seat belt light,

966
01:59:00,808 --> 01:59:05,643
Flight time to Caracas, Venezuela,
this evening is five hours and 32 minutes,

967
01:59:05,746 --> 01:59:10,274
While in your seat, the captain asks
that you keep your seat belt fastened,

968
01:59:16,257 --> 01:59:18,054
This guy's a teacher?

969
01:59:18,693 --> 01:59:20,593
At a community college.

970
02:01:00,628 --> 02:01:01,822
Hey!

971
02:03:05,986 --> 02:03:08,614
- She heard a button pop.
- What?

972
02:03:14,862 --> 02:03:16,762
She heard a button pop.

973
02:03:24,438 --> 02:03:26,998
Was it raining when we searched the scene?

974
02:03:27,108 --> 02:03:28,473
Three years ago?

975
02:03:28,709 --> 02:03:30,643
What are we doing here?

976
02:03:56,837 --> 02:03:59,704
Why don't you act like a cop?
Grab the other side.

977
02:03:59,807 --> 02:04:01,001
You're out of your mind.

978
02:04:03,377 --> 02:04:05,072
- Ready?
- Yeah.

979
02:04:08,883 --> 02:04:09,907
You got it?

980
02:04:25,232 --> 02:04:27,166
You really thought you were gonna find it?
